Comments and Suggestions for Authors

This paper formalizes the structure of normal CPS/IIoT telemetry as ten
Massive, Implicit, Imbalanced Multimodality (MIIM) assumptions (A1=E2=80=93=
A10) and
introduces LatAD, an unsupervised detector that learns a latent
Gaussian-mixture regime clustering, scores anomalies by latent density and
a rare-regime-safe nearest-component likelihood, and factorizes the density
over correlation-community subsystems combined by cohesion-weighted Higher
Criticism with an auto-gated reconstruction residual head. Under raw
point-wise metrics and difficulty stratification on WADI, HAI, and SWaT,
LatAD achieves the best overall AUROC and leads the difficult anomaly
subsets, with a statistically significant gain on HAI over
reconstruction-based deep detectors such as USAD and TranAD.

The research content of the paper is very interesting, but the reviewers
have raised the following issues or suggestions:

   1. When an abbreviation first appears in the abstract or main text, its
   full form should be provided, e.g., LatAD, IIoT, CPS, SCADA, etc.
   2. The abstract spends most of its length introducing the problems of
   existing anomaly detection methods, while providing very little
   introduction to the principle of the paper's core contribution, LatAD.
   Please highlight the technical contributions of this paper in the abstra=
ct.
   3. The logic of the Introduction is not clear enough and should be
   carefully revised. In the first paragraph, the last sentence, "This pape=
r
   detects them by XXX," should be deleted. The paper's contributions shoul=
d
   not be introduced in the first paragraph of the Introduction. It is
   suggested to add background on cyber-physical systems in the first
   paragraph.
   4. On Page 2, line 71, "the task is often framed as XXX"=E2=80=94what ta=
sk does
   "the task" specifically refer to? Please state it clearly.
   5. The paper states that modeling and evaluation are "two obstacles that
   have obscured this failure mode." Has LatAD made contributions to both
   aspects? What specific problem is LatAD proposed to address, or what
   existing method does it improve? Please explain clearly.
   6. The structure of the Related Work section also has major problems and
   should be revised. First, the definition of anomaly detection in the fir=
st
   sentence should be moved to the Introduction. Second, since LatAD is the
   authors' novel work, it should not be described in detail in Related Wor=
k.
   It is suggested to delete: the last sentence of the first paragraph, "La=
tAD
   sits squarely in this line XXX"; the last sentence of Section 2.1, "LatA=
D
   addresses a complementary IIoT problem XXX"; and the last paragraph of
   Section 2.2, "LatAD adopts this critique as XXX." Section 2.3 is entirel=
y
   an introduction to LatAD and needs to be rewritten. Section 2.5 is
   suggested to be deleted.
   7. Add a system model diagram or an application scenario diagram that
   shows at which stage of the Industrial IoT the proposed LatAD method
   collects data and performs anomaly detection.
   8. What is the relationship between the MIIM presented in Section 3 and
   the LatAD detector presented in Section 4? Are they studied independentl=
y
   or closely related? Please add an explanation of their relationship.
   9. The readability of Section 4 needs to be improved. Sections 4.1 to
   4.4 barely mention LatAD in the main text, making it unclear which part =
of
   the LatAD detector pipeline each corresponds to. Which parts of the LatA=
D
   detector pipeline do the representation stage and scoring stage correspo=
nd
   to? Please add a figure to introduce the LatAD workflow.
   10. Is VaDE + density head + residual head fitted separately for each
   community? Or is the encoder shared? The paper does not report training
   time, GPU memory, or inference latency, which is critical for IIoT edge
   deployment.
   11. The symbol z denotes a latent variable in =C2=A74.3 but a standardiz=
ed
   per-channel value in =C2=A75.3. Although the paper includes the sentence=
 "here z
   is a standardized per-channel value, not the latent z of =C2=A74.3," the=
 symbol
   conflict is still serious. It is suggested to replace z with another sym=
bol
   in =C2=A74.2 or =C2=A75.3.
   12. Typesetting issues: Some paragraphs begin flush left, while others
   are indented. Please unify the format. None of the equations in the pape=
r
   are numbered.

